-- Updated Capricorn entries — planet-specific
DELETE FROM kb_planet_in_sign WHERE sign = 'Capricorn';

INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES

('Sun', 'Capricorn', 'You are the achiever and the architect of your own empire. Your core identity is built on responsibility, competence, and the drive to reach the summit. You don''t need external validation because your internal standards are exacting.',
'Your life follows a deliberate upward trajectory—each goal builds on the last. You''re naturally drawn to positions of authority and respect, moving steadily through life''s hierarchy. Status and genuine accomplishment matter deeply to you, and you earn both through sheer commitment.',
'You attract people who value your steadiness and reliability. In relationships, you''re the dependable one, the partner others lean on. You inspire respect more than spontaneous affection, though your loyalty runs as deep as stone.',
'The challenge is allowing yourself to play, relax, and be imperfect. You can become so focused on the climb that you forget to enjoy the view. Learning to warm up emotionally and show vulnerability without losing your power is essential.',
'Your growth comes through understanding that success without meaning feels hollow. Mentor others, connect your ambition to something larger than status. When you lead with integrity as your cornerstone, you become truly formidable.',
'Dane Rudhyar - "The Astrology of Fate"; Stephen Arroyo - "The Practice and Profession of Astrology"'),

('Moon', 'Capricorn', 'You feel most secure when you have structure and can rely on yourself. Your emotional needs are practical—you want stability, respect, and the knowledge that you''ve earned your place. Feelings run deep but you express them through loyalty and care.',
'You seek emotional safety through self-sufficiency and professional achievement. Your inner world is orderly; you process feelings methodically rather than impulsively. You build emotional walls not from coldness but from respect for boundaries.',
'You''re the steady, reliable partner who shows love through consistent presence and practical support. You''re uncomfortable with emotional dramatics but profoundly dedicated to those you commit to. Others sense your competence and trust you with their vulnerabilities.',
'The challenge is the detriment of the Moon here—your emotional needs feel at odds with Capricornian control. You can suppress feelings until they crystallize into resentment. Learning to honor your sensitivity without losing your grounding is crucial.',
'Your growth emerges when you embrace that emotions are not weakness but wisdom. Allow yourself to feel sadness, joy, and fear without judgment. When you soften your armor slightly, you discover that vulnerability deepens rather than threatens your security.',
'Liz Greene - "The Outer Planets and Their Cycles"; Donna Cunningham - "Moon Sign Astrology"'),

('Mercury', 'Capricorn', 'Your mind is sharp, practical, and strategic. You think three steps ahead and distrust vagueness or wishful thinking. Communication is direct and purposeful—you have little patience for small talk, preferring conversations that accomplish something.',
'Your thinking style emphasizes logic, tradition, and what works in the real world. You''re a natural researcher who investigates thoroughly before forming opinions. Skepticism serves you well; you believe evidence, not hype.',
'In dialogue, you''re respectful and clear, though others sometimes find you overly serious. Your words carry weight because you don''t waste them. You''re excellent at explaining complex systems and teaching others through structured, patient instruction.',
'The challenge is rigidity—you can dismiss ideas that don''t fit your framework. Your need for order can make you dismissive of imagination or abstract thinking. Learning to entertain possibilities, even unlikely ones, expands your wisdom.',
'Your growth comes through recognizing that the best ideas combine tradition with innovation. Curiosity about unconventional thinking strengthens rather than weakens your logic. When you listen to intuition alongside reason, your strategic mind becomes genius.',
'Donna Cunningham - "The Astrological Mercury"; Steven Forrest - "The Only Astrology Book You''ll Ever Need"'),

('Venus', 'Capricorn', 'Your love is quiet, steady, and built on respect. You''re drawn to partners with substance, status, and authenticity. Attraction grows slowly—you''re not swept away by passion alone but by someone''s character, intelligence, and proven reliability.',
'You express affection through acts of service and long-term commitment. You''re a slow burn in romance; trust and safety must be established first. Once committed, you''re a constant presence, offering stability that others rarely find.',
'You attract mature, accomplished partners who value tradition and depth. You''re most comfortable with someone who understands that love is a commitment, not a transaction. Your loyalty creates the kind of partnership that endures.',
'The challenge is appearing cold or overly practical about love. You can prioritize status or security over genuine connection, or take so long to warm up that others move on. Fear of emotional messiness can keep you isolated.',
'Your growth emerges when you realize love is the highest achievement of all. Allow spontaneity, romance, and play into your partnerships. When you let someone in completely—imperfections and all—you experience the richness you''ve been protecting yourself from.',
'Liz Greene - "Relating"; Robert Hand - "Planets in Composite"'),

('Mars', 'Capricorn', 'Your drive is relentless, strategic, and almost unstoppable. Mars is exalted here, giving you the ability to turn ambition into concrete results. You don''t burn bright and fast—you burn steady and long, conquering mountains with patience and power.',
'Your action style is deliberate and controlled. You move toward your goals with the precision of a general planning a campaign. You''re the person who makes five-year plans and actually follows them. Your energy is channeled into what matters most.',
'In competition and conflict, you''re formidable but fair. You don''t provoke fights unnecessarily, but you''ll stand your ground with quiet authority. Others recognize your strength and rarely challenge you directly.',
'The challenge is confusing discipline with inflexibility. You can suppress anger until it becomes icy resentment. Your controlled ambition might manifest as frustration when progress isn''t visible enough or fast enough, even when you''re steady.',
'Your growth comes through channeling your exalted Mars toward service. Use your unstoppable drive to build something that outlasts you. When your ambition serves a greater purpose, your energy becomes genuinely transformative.',
'Robert Hand - "Planets in Transit"; Stephen Arroyo - "The Practice and Profession of Astrology"'),

('Jupiter', 'Capricorn', 'Your luck is earned, not given. Jupiter is in fall here, meaning growth feels restricted and expansion must be carefully managed. You don''t believe in free rides. Good fortune comes through discipline, timing, and smart choices.',
'Your path to abundance is unconventional—you succeed by being more practical, more patient, and more strategic than the competition. You''re suspicious of overnight wealth and prefer slow accumulation. Your luck multiplies when you invest in systems and relationships.',
'You attract mentors and partners who appreciate your serious approach to growth. Your greatest luck comes from people who value integrity over flash. Collaboration with others who share your work ethic opens doors you couldn''t access alone.',
'The challenge is feeling unlucky or restricted, especially watching others succeed more easily. You can become overly pessimistic about opportunities or assume limitations that don''t actually exist. Envy of others'' seemingly effortless abundance may surface.',
'Your growth emerges through trust in your own proven methods. Your path may be longer, but it''s solid. When you embrace that your success is unshakeable precisely because it''s earned, you discover that true abundance isn''t about having more—it''s about having enough, built to last.',
'Stephen Arroyo - "The Practice and Profession of Astrology"; Liz Greene - "The Outer Planets and Their Cycles"'),

('Saturn', 'Capricorn', 'Saturn rules Capricorn—you are on home turf. This is the ultimate expression of discipline, integrity, and responsibility. Your life lessons are deep but they forge you into something unbreakable. You''re here to master discipline and build legacy.',
'Your life pattern is methodical mastery. Saturn here gives you the patience to develop real expertise and the wisdom to know that shortcuts crumble. You''re drawn to institutions, traditions, and systems that have proven themselves over time.',
'In relationships, you''re the stable presence, the one others can build their lives around. You take commitments seriously and expect the same in return. Your love is expressed through reliability and the unglamorous work of showing up.',
'The challenge is becoming too rigid, cold, or pessimistic. You can mistake harshness for honesty and withholding for wisdom. Learning when to loosen your grip and allow others their own journey is essential.',
'Your growth comes through recognizing that structure serves joy, not the reverse. You''re here to build something lasting—systems, wisdom, institutions that help others. When you lead with compassion alongside your discipline, you become an elder others genuinely respect.',
'Stephen Arroyo - "Astrology, Psychology, and the Four Elements"; Dane Rudhyar - "The Astrology of Fate"'),

('Uranus', 'Capricorn', 'You are generational rebels with a traditional twist. Your revolution is strategic and structural, not flashy. You see what''s broken in systems and imagine efficient, radical alternatives. Your innovation challenges others to think differently about tradition.',
'Your generational pattern emphasizes reform over revolution. You work within institutions to transform them, or you create new structures that prove to be more effective than the old ways. Change feels less like rebellion and more like inevitable progress.',
'You attract like-minded thinkers who recognize that the future requires both vision and practicality. You collaborate with others who understand that real change requires patience and smart strategy. Your network is built on shared purpose, not mere socializing.',
'The challenge is the tension between Uranus''s need to break free and Capricorn''s need for stability. You can feel trapped by expectations or frustrated that change isn''t coming fast enough. Your unconventional impulses may feel at odds with your responsibilities.',
'Your growth emerges through embracing that true innovation builds on what''s solid. Your generational task is to ask: "What traditions deserve to transform and what traditions deserve protecting?" When you balance reform with respect for proven systems, you lead genuine evolution.',
'Liz Greene - "The Outer Planets and Their Cycles"; Steven Forrest - "The Outer Planets as Psychological Forces"'),

('Neptune', 'Capricorn', 'You are generational dreamers grounded in reality. Neptune here softens Capricorn''s hardness, revealing transcendent purpose beneath practical goals. Your generation envisions spiritual transformation within or alongside material systems. You believe the sacred and the structural can coexist.',
'Your generational pattern emphasizes meaning-making in institutions. You''re drawn to spirituality, art, and compassion as tools for social change. You sense what humanity needs beyond profit and prestige, even as you build practical pathways to those deeper values.',
'You attract communities bound by shared ideals and vision. Your gift is translating spiritual or humanitarian purpose into structures others can actually build. You''re comfortable holding both reverence and responsibility simultaneously.',
'The challenge is confusion about what''s truly spiritual versus what''s escapism. You can become disillusioned when reality doesn''t match your vision. Learning to create beauty and meaning within limitations, not in opposition to them, is essential.',
'Your growth emerges through recognizing that the most transcendent gift your generation offers is proving that integrity and imagination can build together. When you trust that meaning can be embedded in systems—that every institution can reflect the sacred—you become a bridge between worlds.',
'Steven Forrest - "The Outer Planets as Psychological Forces"; Dane Rudhyar - "An Astrological Mandala"'),

('Pluto', 'Capricorn', 'You are generational alchemists of power and control. Pluto here demands your generation face truth about systems, hierarchy, and what deserves to die so renewal can begin. Your transformation involves restructuring what''s foundational. You wield influence quietly but intensely.',
'Your generational pattern emphasizes examining the roots of authority itself. You''re drawn to investigating what truly holds power and questioning whether existing hierarchies deserve their position. Your work involves necessary destruction of false foundations and rebuilding on bedrock truth.',
'You attract people who sense your psychological depth and transformative potential. Others feel they can trust you with their darkest truths because you don''t flinch. Your power lies not in domination but in understanding.',
'The challenge is the temptation to control outcomes or manipulate systems toward your vision. You can become obsessed with hidden power or corporate structures. Learning that true transformation requires surrender as much as strategy is crucial.',
'Your growth emerges when you recognize that your generation''s deepest task is honest reckoning. You''re here to ask: "What systems are dying and what needs to be born?" When you combine your power with integrity, you midwife transformation that actually serves the future.',
'Liz Greene - "The Outer Planets and Their Cycles"; Dane Rudhyar - "The Astrology of Fate"');
